.TH ORO-HCI 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:hci \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:hci'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Provides a low\-level interface to the Linux Bluetooth Host Controller Interface (HCI) via the `HCI_CHANNEL_USER` socket. This API is intended for advanced use cases where direct access to the controller is required; higher\-level Bluetooth features should prefer the standard runtime Bluetooth services when possible.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBlistAdapters()\fR
Enumerate available HCI adapters on the host.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIHCIAdapter[]\fR
.TP
\fBgetAdapter(devId)\fR
Retrieve information for a specific adapter.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdevId\fR (number; required) Adapter identifier (e.g. `0` for `hci0`)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIHCIAdapter\fR
.TP
\fBsetAdapterState(devId, up)\fR
Enable or disable an adapter by bringing it up or down.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdevId\fR (number; required) Adapter identifier
.br
\fIup\fR (boolean; required) When `true`, powers the adapter; otherwise powers it off
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI{ devId: number, up: boolean }\fR
.TP
\fBHCISocket (extends EventEmitter)\fR
Low\-level socket for interacting with a Bluetooth controller via HCI.
.TP
\fBconstructor(options)\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (number \\| { devId?: number }; optional) Optional adapter identifier or configuration object.
.TP
\fBclosed()\fR
Indicates whether the socket has been closed.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBwrite(chunk)\fR
Write an HCI packet to the controller.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIchunk\fR (ArrayBufferView \\| ArrayBuffer \\| Buffer \\| string \\| number[]; required) HCI packet bytes.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR Number of bytes written.
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Stop receiving data and close the underlying socket.
.TP
\fBlistAdapters()\fR
Convenience helper mirroring {@link listAdapters}.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIHCIAdapter[]\fR
.TP
\fBgetAdapter(devId)\fR
Convenience helper mirroring {@link getAdapter}.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdevId\fR (number; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIHCIAdapter\fR
.TP
\fBsetAdapterState(devId, up)\fR
Convenience helper mirroring {@link setAdapterState}.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdevId\fR (number; required)
.br
\fIup\fR (boolean; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI{ devId: number, up: boolean }\fR
